==Battleground==
*1 [[Mooth]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Glowstick Guys]] spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Metal Hippoe]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*10 [[Kroxo]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Crazed Moneko (Enemy)|Crazed Moneko]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Super Metal Hippoe]] spawns.
**3 [[Glowstick Guys]] spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**1 [[Maawth]] spawns.
**3 [[Kroxo]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**3 [[Glowstick Guys]] spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Kroxo]]s spawn, delay 20~33.33 seconds<sup>600f~1,000f</sup>.
**3 [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Metal Hippoe]] spawns.
**3 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Glowstick Guys]] spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] have been buffed enough to where you should have most of the [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] before attempting this.

[[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|Anti-Alien Cats]] such as [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] are recommended to take out the Kroxos and Imperator Sael. Because Maawth outranges Macho Leg, [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] and/or [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]] may be helpful additions as well, and [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] can be used to snipe him and Crazed Moneko from behind the frontlines. A [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitter]] such as [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]], [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]], or [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]] will be necessary to defeat Super Metal Hippoe in order to reach Crazed Moneko. [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave-immune cats]] or [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]] are able to survive or negate her third attack and open Crazed Moneko to damage, but are far from necessary.

